{"path": "/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12876/comments", "params": {"per_page": 100}, "body": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/3980035050", "html_url": "https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12876#issuecomment-3980035050", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12876", "id": 3980035050, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBWBCuM7tOoPq", "user": {"login": "yangbaechu", "id": 45089264, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDg5MjY0", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45089264?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangbaechu", "html_url": "https://github.com/yangbaechu", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangbaechu/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangbaechu/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangbaechu/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangbaechu/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangbaechu/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangbaechu/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangbaechu/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangbaechu/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yangbaechu/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-03-01T14:05:14Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-01T14:05:14Z", "body": "I found that `before` model validators are wrapped inside `model_schema(...)`, while `after`/`wrap` validators sit outside it. The `model` validator already has a path that returns an existing exact instance unchanged under `revalidate_instances='never'`, but the outer `after`/`wrap` validators still run because they always apply their callback to the inner validator result. My plan is to fix this in `pydantic-core` by making the outer model-validator wrappers skip `after`/`wrap` on that exact existing-instance path under `revalidate_instances='never'`, with a focused regression test. Does that sound like the right direction?", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/3980035050/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}]}